WEBVTT

00:03.090 --> 00:12.370
CULTURE FEST

00:06.200 --> 00:09.070
Well, it's voluntary participation for seniors,

00:09.070 --> 00:12.370
so what shall we do?
I'd like to hear your opinions.

00:12.570 --> 00:14.630
Aw, it's such a pain.

00:14.870 --> 00:16.430
Who's gonna do it?

00:16.940 --> 00:19.340
It's okay, we'll only get tired.

00:18.610 --> 00:22.910
What are you saying, you wimpy weaklings?!

00:23.350 --> 00:25.720
The culture fest is the best part of school life!

00:25.880 --> 00:28.750
A paradise! Extraterritorial rights! An informal zone!

00:29.150 --> 00:32.750
You can abandon yourself to boisterous merrymaking and unleash your libido!

00:33.090 --> 00:36.960
You can realize your ambitions in the name of a just cause!

00:37.330 --> 00:39.360
To not even take advantage of this golden opportunity...

00:39.460 --> 00:41.520
...and settle to be nothing more than observers...

00:41.600 --> 00:43.330
...is the decision of a fool!

00:44.370 --> 00:45.390
H-he's right.

00:45.470 --> 00:47.170
It's the last time, after all.

00:46.710 --> 00:48.140
You want to do something?

01:00.550 --> 01:02.110
And so!

01:03.890 --> 01:08.490
Senior year, Class D will set up a cafe!

01:08.490 --> 01:11.550
Culture Fest Executive

01:08.490 --> 01:11.550
Committee President

01:15.500 --> 01:17.370
I shall pray for your success!

01:20.240 --> 01:22.610
Well, then, who'll be in charge?

01:25.780 --> 01:29.340
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:29.880 --> 01:32.980
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:32.980 --> 01:36.550
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

01:36.790 --> 01:39.820
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:40.090 --> 01:43.730
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

01:43.730 --> 01:47.300
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:47.300 --> 01:50.670
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

01:50.870 --> 01:54.360
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

01:54.470 --> 01:57.840
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

01:58.040 --> 02:01.450
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

02:01.610 --> 02:06.020
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

02:06.250 --> 02:09.150
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

02:09.450 --> 02:15.390
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

02:15.730 --> 02:22.460
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

02:23.100 --> 02:27.060
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

02:27.140 --> 02:30.280
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

02:30.280 --> 02:34.050
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:34.050 --> 02:37.310
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

02:37.380 --> 02:41.150
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:41.490 --> 02:44.620
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:44.620 --> 02:48.220
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:48.390 --> 02:51.330
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:54.330 --> 03:01.100
THE DISTANCE
BETWEEN THEM

03:01.470 --> 03:03.240
Any candidates?

03:03.940 --> 03:06.780
Are there any volunteers?
I'd like that person to do it.

03:12.080 --> 03:14.020
Kazuki! Kazuki! How 'bout you?

03:14.120 --> 03:15.380
What? Me?

03:15.690 --> 03:17.380
It sounds like a ton of fun!

03:17.520 --> 03:20.720
My old school didn't have a proper culture fest like this.

03:20.830 --> 03:22.120
Don't you want to?

03:22.530 --> 03:23.320
I'm fine.

03:23.530 --> 03:26.790
Why not? There aren't any events for a good while, so what's wrong?!

03:26.930 --> 03:29.370
Someone with time to kill can do it.

03:33.100 --> 03:34.600
Is there anyone?

03:34.870 --> 03:36.270
Nominations are fine, too.

03:38.240 --> 03:39.610
Who'll do it?

03:39.180 --> 03:40.480
I'll pass!

03:42.510 --> 03:43.680
Here!

03:43.080 --> 03:44.340
Yes, Miss Takase.

03:45.350 --> 03:46.940
I think Sendou will do a good job.

03:47.690 --> 03:48.850
What?!

03:54.830 --> 03:56.660
Whoa, I have a lot of e-mail.

03:56.660 --> 03:58.460
CULTURE FEST

03:56.660 --> 03:58.460
SENIOR YEAR

03:56.660 --> 03:58.460
CLASS D PROJECT:

03:56.660 --> 03:58.460
CAFE

03:56.660 --> 03:58.460
IN CHARGE:

03:56.660 --> 03:58.460
KAZUKI SENDOU

04:01.430 --> 04:02.870
Hey, wait, Mizuki!

04:04.400 --> 04:06.460
Why did you nominate me?

04:09.170 --> 04:11.040
Because you looked like you had time to kill.

04:11.040 --> 04:11.980
Wh-wha...

04:11.980 --> 04:13.710
Well, what does it matter?

04:13.780 --> 04:16.680
Just do it. I'll help out, too.

04:16.980 --> 04:18.250
Easy for you to say...

04:18.250 --> 04:20.410
Now that's decided, better have a strategy meeting!

04:20.520 --> 04:21.540
H-hey!

04:21.620 --> 04:24.820
You can't drag your feet 'bout these things. We're goin'.

04:25.060 --> 04:27.460
Let's go! Right, Mizuki?

04:28.130 --> 04:29.530
Y-yeah.

04:33.330 --> 04:35.860
This is about how big the classroom is, right?

04:36.030 --> 04:39.900
We'll put up some cute decorations.
How much should we charge?

04:39.970 --> 04:41.460
And what should we do about food?

04:41.610 --> 04:44.840
The girls can take turns waitin' tables...

04:45.210 --> 04:46.470
Wait.

04:47.180 --> 04:49.080
Nothing's been decided yet.

04:51.580 --> 04:53.310
You say it so simply,

04:53.450 --> 04:55.720
but we have to decide what our goals are first.

04:55.820 --> 04:57.050
Goals?

04:57.220 --> 04:59.250
Like is it important to make a profit?

04:59.390 --> 05:01.920
Or do we just want to have fun playing at setting up shop?

05:02.430 --> 05:05.420
Profit, of course!
Let the money trees blossom!

05:05.660 --> 05:06.760
Right, Mizuki?

05:07.200 --> 05:09.390
What? Yeah...

05:10.070 --> 05:11.760
What is it?

05:12.170 --> 05:13.470
I'd rather...

05:13.570 --> 05:18.200
I'd rather have more fulfillment, like a sense of accomplishment.

05:18.580 --> 05:24.240
Sort of like having the customers' and our enjoyment be the same.

05:24.920 --> 05:28.180
Like the fun of creating something or communicating.

05:28.350 --> 05:31.150
It's sort of vague, and I don't get it.

05:31.590 --> 05:32.820
Well...

05:32.890 --> 05:36.050
In other words, do you mean rather than making profit our sole goal,

05:36.190 --> 05:39.360
you want to enjoy the whole shop experience while we're at it?

05:39.830 --> 05:41.420
Oh, right!

05:41.900 --> 05:45.460
Oh, I can understand that.
Or rather, that's like a given.

05:45.640 --> 05:48.540
But it's tough that we don't have many people.

05:48.770 --> 05:52.770
I'll go ask around.
I'll ask Chinami and Reina.

05:53.140 --> 05:55.910
No! A fried noodle stand style trap!

05:57.220 --> 05:59.980
When business gets slow at a fried noodle stand,

06:00.120 --> 06:02.610
they pour sauce onto the frying surface so it sizzles.

06:02.750 --> 06:04.480
Then it smells real good, right?

06:04.760 --> 06:07.190
When it smells good, everyone stops in their tracks, see?

06:07.190 --> 06:08.990
You win if you can make them stop by.

06:09.790 --> 06:12.800
So, if we send out a vibe like we're havin' fun,

06:12.800 --> 06:14.490
everyone will come to us!

06:14.900 --> 06:16.700
Oh, I get it.

06:17.600 --> 06:18.970
Well, just watch.

06:19.170 --> 06:22.740
And so, the First
Triumvirate was formed...

06:22.210 --> 06:23.680
Here.

06:22.740 --> 06:25.540
by Caesar, Crassus, and Pompey.

06:24.680 --> 06:26.010
"ROUGH SKETCH OF STORE"

06:25.540 --> 06:28.510
And the Second
Triumvirate was formed...

06:28.510 --> 06:31.380
...by Octavius, Antonius, and Lepidus.

06:33.280 --> 06:34.750
What should we do about food?

06:35.220 --> 06:37.520
We can't shop for supplies if we don't settle on a menu.

06:37.690 --> 06:39.660
And we can't do anything too complicated.

06:40.090 --> 06:42.530
Are we allowed to use stove tops in the classroom?

06:42.830 --> 06:44.890
I'll have to check on that with Taishi.

06:45.360 --> 06:48.090
How about cookies? You can bake and stockpile them.

06:48.230 --> 06:49.230
Chinami!

06:49.230 --> 06:52.140
Also, if it's for about 2 days, donuts might be good, too.

06:52.470 --> 06:54.500
We could serve store-bought soy sauce crackers, too.

06:55.240 --> 06:57.500
Why don't we just go for a set menu?

06:57.780 --> 06:59.870
So, we play it up like it's a deal, right?

07:00.980 --> 07:02.570
All right, let's go with that!

07:03.450 --> 07:05.510
<i>PROJECT PLAN</i>

07:03.850 --> 07:04.820
Good!

07:05.280 --> 07:05.510
PERMISSION

07:05.280 --> 07:05.510
GRANTED

07:07.220 --> 07:08.520
Don't just say it's good, Taishi.

07:08.620 --> 07:11.450
Look at the content and the budget for real.

07:11.620 --> 07:13.390
You sure it's okay to grant permission like that?

07:13.520 --> 07:14.320
Of course!

07:15.290 --> 07:19.460
I have the Asahi Sakurai super-gorgeous, ultimate live concert,

07:19.530 --> 07:22.860
MK-2 to prepare, a most important task.

07:23.270 --> 07:27.600
For the fate of the concert rides entirely upon my shoulders!

07:27.870 --> 07:30.900
Or what? Don't you want me to give you permission?

07:31.210 --> 07:33.200
I'll take it back if you wish it.

07:33.340 --> 07:35.870
No, permission is good. Later.

07:39.920 --> 07:41.550
So, he has not realized it yet.

07:42.490 --> 07:43.960
But that is fine, too.

07:53.500 --> 07:55.260
What's with Taishi?

07:55.600 --> 07:57.900
He's doing exactly what he wants to do.

07:58.600 --> 07:59.370
It's not fair!

08:03.140 --> 08:05.040
Owowow...

08:04.380 --> 08:05.600
Chisa!

08:06.080 --> 08:07.980
Oh, it's you, Sir!

08:08.480 --> 08:09.780
S-sorry.

08:11.080 --> 08:13.350
It is Chisa's fault for being in a hurry.

08:17.090 --> 08:20.080
I guess your class is doing a cafe.

08:20.320 --> 08:22.520
Yeah, drop by if you like.

08:22.830 --> 08:25.350
Yes, I will definitely, definitely come!

08:25.930 --> 08:29.300
Chisa's group is doing a research presentation on printing.

08:29.630 --> 08:32.130
From Gutenberg to the
Tsukamoto Printers!

08:32.270 --> 08:33.740
Please come see us.

08:34.110 --> 08:35.570
S-sure.

08:36.740 --> 08:38.370
We got permission.

08:42.910 --> 08:46.540
Well? It's the waitress uniform.
It's a trial version, though.

08:47.050 --> 08:48.350
Yeah, not bad...

08:48.650 --> 08:51.490
You're not very encouragin'.
Is that all you have to say?

08:51.690 --> 08:54.750
Well, I don't really know much about these things.

08:55.030 --> 08:57.460
There's nothin' to know or not know.

08:57.460 --> 08:59.800
Is it good or bad? Do you like it or not?

09:03.700 --> 09:05.290
Yeah, I think it's good.

09:06.970 --> 09:08.070
All right!

09:08.070 --> 09:10.770
Sendou, how are we going to get supplies?

09:12.240 --> 09:13.910
Won't we find things in the phone book?

09:14.280 --> 09:18.270
Y-yeah, how about calling around and asking for prices first?

09:18.450 --> 09:21.110
Say, the design for the menu is okay like this, right?

09:21.390 --> 09:22.410
That looks nice!

09:22.750 --> 09:25.420
Then, let's check for any misspellings...

09:25.520 --> 09:28.390
...and if there aren't any, go make copies. Maybe about 20 copies?

09:28.690 --> 09:30.360
How is the food going?

09:30.500 --> 09:32.860
We'll have a list made by the time we need to go shoppin'.

09:33.000 --> 09:35.520
So, what's goin' on with assignin' cookin' duties?

09:35.870 --> 09:37.530
Oh, I'll have that soon.

09:37.840 --> 09:39.800
I want to go buy some balsa wood...

09:40.070 --> 09:41.270
Oh, right.

09:41.270 --> 09:43.800
Budget

09:44.310 --> 09:46.540
Don't forget to get a receipt.

09:46.940 --> 09:48.470
Okay, got it.

09:51.820 --> 09:53.410
My brother, Kazuki.

09:54.050 --> 09:56.320
Your powers of planning and execution.

09:56.490 --> 09:58.580
How did you come by them?

09:58.660 --> 10:01.060
There will surely come a time when you realize the answer.

10:01.160 --> 10:05.360
You can never escape from the joy of creation!

10:18.710 --> 10:19.570
Okay!

10:20.280 --> 10:30.280
Days Until the

10:20.280 --> 10:30.280
Culture Fest

10:51.110 --> 10:56.070
Days Until the Culture Fest

11:08.660 --> 11:11.150
Welcome to Senior Year Class D

11:14.070 --> 11:17.000
Welcome to Senior Year Class D

11:19.240 --> 11:22.140
I had no idea how things would turn out in the beginning, but...

11:25.740 --> 11:27.040
You're still here?

11:27.040 --> 11:28.980
I thought I'd iron these.

11:29.480 --> 11:30.810
What about you, Kazuki?

11:30.880 --> 11:34.440
Yeah, well, sort of checking things over one last time.

11:37.020 --> 11:38.220
Say...
Say...

11:41.590 --> 11:42.990
What is it?

11:44.700 --> 11:49.400
Shoot! Shoot! Shoot! I forgot about somethin' really important!

11:49.730 --> 11:50.860
Forgot? Forgot what?

11:51.100 --> 11:52.660
A store sign and flyers!

11:52.770 --> 11:55.260
We've forgotten about a store sign for the front and flyers!

11:56.970 --> 11:57.780
What'll we do?

11:57.780 --> 12:01.140
Knowin' you, I thought you'd have had them ready long ago.

12:01.480 --> 12:02.810
No, I didn't do it.

12:03.010 --> 12:04.280
That's not good!

12:04.350 --> 12:06.680
I told you before at the exhibition and spot sale, remember?

12:06.750 --> 12:09.720
You absolutely need somethin' to draw the eyes of your customers!

12:11.490 --> 12:13.320
You think we can manage somehow if we start now?

12:13.420 --> 12:16.020
We still have paint and paper, right?

12:16.130 --> 12:17.320
Y-yeah.

12:19.030 --> 12:20.760
What're ya doin'? We gotta hurry!

12:34.780 --> 12:36.580
I'm sorry, but I...

12:42.750 --> 12:44.450
I'll do it!

12:44.860 --> 12:45.910
What?!

12:45.990 --> 12:47.250
You, Mizuki?

12:47.320 --> 12:48.690
Yeah, leave it to me.

12:49.060 --> 12:51.090
But Mizuki, you...

12:51.530 --> 12:52.690
I'll do it!

13:12.920 --> 13:13.680
Kazuki...

13:14.220 --> 13:15.050
Can't draw it?

13:17.560 --> 13:18.350
I'll help you.

13:28.470 --> 13:29.760
Here.

13:40.110 --> 13:41.700
You think that'll do it?

13:43.210 --> 13:45.650
What? Don't like it?

13:45.650 --> 13:47.550
No, that's not it. You know...

13:51.160 --> 13:52.090
I'm glad.

13:52.320 --> 13:53.380
Huh?

13:54.020 --> 13:57.720
I thought that you might come,

13:58.860 --> 14:02.200
but I was beginning to think you might not.

14:04.740 --> 14:07.710
In the end, I like you best when you're doing something.

14:09.070 --> 14:11.140
It's more like you if you're frantically rushing about...

14:11.140 --> 14:14.310
...rather than being spaced out with too much free time.

14:20.420 --> 14:21.250
Um...

14:21.250 --> 14:24.710
Mizuki! I brought you some snacks!

14:26.960 --> 14:29.480
Kazuki! So, you're here after all.

14:29.560 --> 14:30.860
Wh-what?

14:31.330 --> 14:35.600
You were worried, right?
About the cafe that is!

14:37.430 --> 14:41.340
Now, let's get this finished up!

14:41.840 --> 14:42.900
Okay!

14:43.640 --> 14:44.840
Hey, that's not right!

14:50.710 --> 14:53.810
Call out to the customers brightly and with spirit!

14:53.920 --> 14:54.580
Yeah!

14:54.920 --> 14:58.820
They're payin' us, so do your best to make them happy!

14:59.160 --> 14:59.820
Yeah!

15:00.190 --> 15:01.560
All right, open shop!

15:13.270 --> 15:18.710
Hello! I'm Asahi Sakurai!
Everyone, here we go!

15:22.980 --> 15:29.210
<i>I just can't be still at all. Why?</i>
<i>Ite mo Tatte mo Irarenai Doushite</i>

15:24.880 --> 15:26.650
Yoyomori High School Culture Fest

15:26.650 --> 15:28.590
Bazaar Area

15:30.490 --> 15:34.630
<i>My feet won't touch the ground.</i>
<i>Ashiga Chi ni Tsukanai Nante</i>

15:31.190 --> 15:34.160
Goldfish Scooping

15:34.630 --> 15:36.960
<i>No way, right?</i>
<i>Masaka ne</i>

15:37.190 --> 15:40.160
Original Dance

15:37.830 --> 15:41.930
<i>I just can't be by myself.</i>
<i>Watashiga Watashi de Irarenai</i>

15:41.930 --> 15:45.560
<i>It's because he's nearby.</i>
<i>Aitsu ga Soba nilru kara ne</i>

15:46.140 --> 15:49.340
<i>I become tongue-tied. You're kidding, right?</i>
<i>Mukuchi ni Naru no Uso Deshou</i>

15:46.470 --> 15:47.670
Welcome!

15:47.670 --> 15:50.340
How would you like some

15:47.670 --> 15:50.340
delicious coffee or tea?

15:49.340 --> 15:52.140
<i>It's because I fell in love, isn't it?</i>
<i>Koi Shita kara nano ne</i>

15:50.910 --> 15:54.480
We have a wonderful cafe set

15:50.910 --> 15:54.480
up in senior year Class D.

15:54.980 --> 15:56.280
Please come visit us.

16:00.280 --> 16:01.580
Hello.

16:02.920 --> 16:04.010
Thanks for comin'!

16:04.490 --> 16:07.250
We'll be open until 4 o'clock, so come again!

16:10.330 --> 16:12.590
Oh, it's you, country panda.

16:12.660 --> 16:14.690
Look at you, here, dressed like that.

16:15.000 --> 16:16.830
You must have a lot of free time.

16:17.070 --> 16:20.800
Hey, right back at you.
What'd you come here for?

16:21.240 --> 16:24.340
What?! Grr! I heard you were doing this cheap stuff...

16:24.340 --> 16:26.610
...because your doujinshi weren't selling.

16:26.610 --> 16:30.310
So, I came all this way, just for you, especially to see you.

16:30.650 --> 16:33.210
So, you've got nothin' better to do after all.

16:33.620 --> 16:36.280
No! Like I said, the great and cute Eimi...

16:36.350 --> 16:38.920
...came to see the country panda's pitiful, miserable state...

16:38.020 --> 16:40.120
Yeah, yeah. Table for one!

16:38.920 --> 16:42.320
H-hey, what are you doing? Does this shop force its business on customers?

16:45.830 --> 16:48.420
Let's see. Table for three.
Thank you for waiting.

16:48.630 --> 16:50.070
Please take that table right over there.

16:50.600 --> 16:52.760
Let's see, next...

16:54.240 --> 16:55.970
What a busy shop!

16:57.140 --> 16:58.610
Thanks for waiting.

17:03.010 --> 17:04.410
Oh, it's delicious.

17:04.750 --> 17:08.150
I'm glad you think so.
I'm sorry it's so crowded.

17:08.320 --> 17:13.490
Not at all, because it is a very nice atmosphere.

17:14.020 --> 17:16.050
And I think it is very like you.

17:16.360 --> 17:17.490
What?

17:18.330 --> 17:19.560
Hey, there you are!

17:20.030 --> 17:21.730
We're here, Sendou!

17:21.930 --> 17:25.560
Sorry. Stay as long as you want. Refills are free.

17:25.770 --> 17:26.570
Okay.

17:27.140 --> 17:28.260
Welcome.

17:28.410 --> 17:31.270
Oh, please! You're totally playing the waiter!

17:31.610 --> 17:34.280
It looks good. What's this a cosplay of?

17:34.280 --> 17:35.800
It's our school uniform!

17:36.250 --> 17:39.410
I'm just kidding, okay?
I want caramel milk tea.

17:39.720 --> 17:42.850
I'll take the oolong tea and fortune cookie set.

17:43.120 --> 17:44.950
Are the cookies handmade?

17:45.020 --> 17:46.920
The shop is really cute.

17:49.660 --> 17:52.820
I see, I had no idea such a thing had happened.

17:53.900 --> 17:56.200
He's cheerful now, because he's busy,

17:56.900 --> 17:59.960
but he might go back to being like that again when it's over.

18:00.900 --> 18:02.370
It'll be fine.

18:02.540 --> 18:03.200
What?

18:03.810 --> 18:07.800
I think Mr. Kazuki only got a little lost on his way.

18:08.480 --> 18:13.820
But I think he'll soon realize which direction he should take.

18:14.320 --> 18:15.880
I hope you're right.

18:16.650 --> 18:19.320
But how do you know that?

18:21.430 --> 18:22.660
This flyer.

18:22.660 --> 18:25.130
Senior Year

18:22.660 --> 18:25.130
Class D

18:22.660 --> 18:25.130
Cafe

18:22.660 --> 18:25.130
"A tasty shop

18:22.660 --> 18:25.130
with tea and

18:22.660 --> 18:25.130
handmade

18:22.660 --> 18:25.130
cookies."

18:25.230 --> 18:27.630
I can see his confidence in it.

18:28.100 --> 18:29.230
Thanks.

18:29.330 --> 18:30.960
Thank you very much.

18:42.810 --> 18:44.340
Why don't you rest a little?

18:45.880 --> 18:48.250
I'll take a break when it quiets down a little.

18:48.450 --> 18:49.920
It's still busy right now.

18:54.260 --> 18:55.490
Why?

18:56.760 --> 18:58.520
Why did you change your mind?

18:58.730 --> 19:00.560
You weren't enthusiastic about it at the beginning.

19:01.800 --> 19:03.700
Why? Well, that's because...

19:03.700 --> 19:06.470
What? It's not just about making money, right?

19:06.740 --> 19:10.940
Well, sure I'll be happy if we make a lot, but you're right.

19:12.080 --> 19:14.550
In the end, it's just fun and I enjoy it.

19:15.180 --> 19:16.840
Making things like this.

19:17.580 --> 19:20.350
Or rather, there's no point in doing it if you don't enjoy it.

19:20.780 --> 19:23.810
And to enjoy it, you have to first get interested.

19:26.190 --> 19:28.420
You're the one who got me into this.

19:28.890 --> 19:32.390
You made me help with the store sign and draw the flyers. What's up?

19:32.700 --> 19:34.030
That's true.

19:34.160 --> 19:35.460
Yes, it is.

19:36.770 --> 19:39.070
Now, just a little more to go!

19:39.740 --> 19:40.800
Yeah!

19:45.440 --> 19:46.740
A tasty shop with tea and handmade cookies

19:46.740 --> 19:48.910
Senior Year Class D

19:46.740 --> 19:48.910
Cafe

19:53.450 --> 19:56.410
Yoyomori High School

19:53.450 --> 19:56.410
Culture Fest

19:54.350 --> 19:56.410
<i>This is an announcement</i> <i>from the executive committee.</i>

19:56.690 --> 20:00.590
<i>The after-party will begin</i> <i>at 5:30 in the schoolyard.</i>

19:57.090 --> 19:58.590
Thank you very much.

20:00.020 --> 20:01.560
Thank you very much.

20:00.960 --> 20:03.260
<i>We ask that the students</i> <i>clean everything up by then.</i>

20:02.730 --> 20:04.280
Thank you very much.

20:05.060 --> 20:06.550
Thank you very much.

20:12.040 --> 20:13.260
Oh, you...

20:13.340 --> 20:14.130
Hello.

20:14.870 --> 20:19.210
Oh, hello. I'm sorry, we're closed.

20:20.010 --> 20:22.880
But there might be some cookies left. Wait here.

20:23.080 --> 20:25.380
It's okay. I've already gotten what I wanted.

20:25.880 --> 20:27.610
Huh? Really?

20:28.020 --> 20:30.250
Yes, something very wonderful.

20:40.000 --> 20:42.470
My friends, was it exciting?!

20:42.700 --> 20:43.970
Yeah!

20:43.970 --> 20:46.460
This is the end! Let's burn out!

20:46.540 --> 20:48.010
Yeah!

20:48.340 --> 20:50.570
Okay! Fire!

21:13.200 --> 21:14.560
It's over.

21:15.770 --> 21:17.700
The sign's been burned.

21:17.970 --> 21:19.270
It's okay.

21:18.840 --> 21:19.460
What?

21:20.070 --> 21:21.470
I can just draw another one.

21:26.580 --> 21:27.550
Say...

21:29.580 --> 21:30.910
Never mind.

21:31.050 --> 21:32.210
What?

21:33.250 --> 21:33.980
What?

21:36.020 --> 21:37.220
I...

21:36.650 --> 21:38.310
So, this is where you were!

21:39.660 --> 21:41.820
What're ya doin'? It's a camp fire.

21:42.160 --> 21:44.320
It's the "Mayim, Mayim". You gotta dance!

21:46.700 --> 21:47.930
Wanna go?

21:49.670 --> 21:50.190
Yeah.

21:51.770 --> 21:53.500
All right! Let's go, let's go!

22:19.700 --> 22:23.900
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:23.900 --> 22:28.400
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:28.540 --> 22:32.910
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:33.110 --> 22:36.980
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:36.980 --> 22:41.120
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:41.120 --> 22:45.390
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:45.560 --> 22:49.960
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:50.090 --> 22:54.130
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:54.130 --> 22:57.700
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:57.700 --> 23:02.610
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:02.740 --> 23:06.280
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:06.280 --> 23:11.680
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:12.750 --> 23:17.220
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:17.220 --> 23:21.220
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:21.220 --> 23:25.760
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:25.760 --> 23:34.730
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:55.330 --> 24:19.480
PREVIEW

23:58.130 --> 24:02.530
Well, the season is turning cold, reminding us winter is coming.

24:02.800 --> 24:04.430
How is everyone doing?

24:04.840 --> 24:10.770
Now, the other day, I watched an animated show called "Comic Party,"

24:11.110 --> 24:12.510
but if I had to say...

24:12.510 --> 24:15.980
No! That's enough! Don't say it, you don't have to say it!

24:15.980 --> 24:17.050
Mizuki, now!

24:17.050 --> 24:18.780
N-n-n-n-next time!

24:19.180 --> 24:20.720
"The Uncertain Future"!

24:20.180 --> 24:25.150
NEXT TIME

24:20.180 --> 24:25.150
THE

24:20.180 --> 24:25.150
UNCERTAIN

24:20.180 --> 24:25.150
FUTURE

24:20.720 --> 24:22.750
Man, that was close.
